---
description: Sidelight project rules (privacy, layout, commands, commits)
alwaysApply: true
---

Follow the full guide in @AGENTS.md. The rules that must never be broken:

- No network calls outside `sidelight-router` and the user's chosen backend. No telemetry.
- Never write captured images to disk; capture exactly one window; never full-screen capture.
- Never put screen text, API keys or personal data in logs, files or test fixtures.
- Output files only when the user enabled saving.
- v1 sends text only to AI backends, never images.
- Platform code only in `packages/reader/src/sidelight_reader/platform/<os>/`, imported lazily.
- No GPL or LGPL dependencies without asking. Use `uv`, never `pip install`.
- Conventional Commits with package scope; no AI attribution lines in commits.
- Run `uv run ruff check --fix`, `uv run ruff format`, `uv run mypy` and tests before calling a change done.
